# Architecture

**{{projectName}}** is a **modular monolith of FastMCP feature sub-servers**. The
shape is mechanically enforced by `dude lint` (the `MCP` rules), so the codebase
stays consistent as it grows.

---

## Layout

```
fastmcp/                         # the service (analogue of a backend/)
├── Dockerfile · start.sh · pyproject.toml
└── app/
    ├── __main__.py              # `python -m app` — wires transport from settings
    ├── server.py                # create_server(): discover + mount feature sub-servers
    ├── config.py                # Settings(BaseSettings) — the ONLY env reader
    ├── core/errors.py           # DomainError (service) → ToolError (client-facing)
    ├── schemas/                 # pydantic models; module name = class prefix
    ├── utils/                   # global helpers (discovery.import_submodules, …)
    ├── features/
    │   └── <feature>/
    │       ├── __init__.py      # exports `server`; auto-imports components
    │       ├── _server.py       # server = FastMCP(name="<feature>")
    │       ├── tools/           # ONE @server.tool per module
    │       ├── resources/       # ONE @server.resource per module
    │       ├── prompts/         # ONE @server.prompt per module
    │       └── utils/           # service.py (pure logic) + helpers
    └── tests/                   # mirrors app/ 1:1
```

## Principles

- **Each bounded context is a feature package** under `app/features/<name>/`
  owning a self-contained `FastMCP` sub-server. `server.create_server()`
  auto-discovers every feature and `mount()`s it into one flat namespace.
- **One tool/resource/prompt per module**, named after the file
  (`tools/add.py` → tool `add`). Component packages auto-import their modules, so
  dropping a file in registers it — no list to maintain.
- **The binding layer is thin**: component modules adapt MCP calls to the
  feature's `utils/service.py` (pure logic). Logic is unit-tested directly; the
  MCP surface is integration-tested via FastMCP's in-memory client.
- **Schemas** live in `app/schemas/` with one PascalCase prefix per module;
  **config** is read only in `config.py`; **client errors** are always `ToolError`.

---

## Lint rules (MCP001–MCP017)

`dude lint` runs these deterministic, AST/structure-level checks. Each has a
prose description under `.claude/rules/MCP/`.

| ID | Rule |
|----|------|
| MCP001 | Required project structure (`app/` + mirrored `tests/`) |
| MCP002 | Feature package shape (`__init__`, `_server`, a component pkg, `utils/`) |
| MCP003 | Sub-server contract (`server = FastMCP(name="<folder>")`, re-export + register) |
| MCP004 | Component placement & purity (decorators only in their package) |
| MCP005 | One component per module, named after the module |
| MCP006 | Docstring required on every component |
| MCP007 | Full type annotations (params + return) |
| MCP008 | Thin binding layer (no I/O imports, no classes, delegate to utils/) |
| MCP009 | Context convention (`ctx: Context`, async when used) |
| MCP010 | Resource URI ↔ params consistency |
| MCP011 | Schema module conventions (BaseModel + filename prefix) |
| MCP012 | snake_case naming (functions, modules, folders) |
| MCP013 | No duplicate tool/prompt names or resource URIs |
| MCP014 | Centralised configuration (`os.environ` only in `config.py`) |
| MCP015 | No `print` (it corrupts the stdio transport) |
| MCP016 | Client-facing errors are `ToolError` |
| MCP017 | 1-to-1 test coverage |

